# Project data conventions

## Layout
Each prospect: `projects/<slug>/` with subdirs `source/`, `screenshots/`, `analysis/`, `strategy/`, `design/`, `data/`, `reports/`, `qa/`, `knowledge/`.

## Key files
- `config.json` — project config (Zod: `lib/schemas/project.ts`)
- `project-status.md` — phase, artifacts, blockers, approved gates
- `source/*.json` — crawl corpus (pages, navigation, documents, forms, tables, images, external-tools, crawl-errors)
- `data/*.json` — structured inventories (company, products, documents, calculators)
- `analysis/*.md` — audits and evidence reports
- `strategy/*.md` — UX and product strategy
- `design/*` — art direction, tokens, copy

## JSON rules
Validate against Zod schemas in `lib/schemas/`. Include `updatedAt` timestamps. Attach `sourceUrl` and `confidence` on factual records.

## Traceability
When updating inventory JSON, preserve existing source URLs. Add open questions rather than guessing missing attributes.

## Status updates
After writing artifacts, append paths to `project-status.md` completed artifacts. Do not delete prior approved content without documented reason.
